hich included a marvellous diamond. He said to his wife, \"Either part with all your jewellery for the sake of Allah, so that I may deposit it in the Baitul Maal or be separated from me. I would not like to live in a house where there is so much wealth.\" His wife replied, \"I can part with a thousand times more wealth, but I cannot leave you.\" She then deposited everything she had in the Baitul Maal. After the death of Umar bin Abdul Aziz, when Yazeed son of Abdul Malik succeeded him as Khalifa, he said to his sister, \"If you like you may have your jewellery back from the Baitul Maal.\" She replied, \"How can the wealth I discarded during my husband''s lifetime, satisfy me after his death.\"\n\nUmar bin Abdul Aziz was on his death-bed when he inquired from the persons round him about the cause of his disease. Someone said, \"People think it is the effect of black magic.\" He said, \"No, it is not magic.\" He then sent for a particular slave of his and said to him, \"What made you poison me?\" He replied, \"One hundred dinaars and a", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 79"}]}'::jsonb);